            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse inverted T waves in a young man with structurally normal heart: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/anec.12013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We discuss a young man with episodes of chest pain and dyspnea accompanied with transient T-wave inversion in precordial and inferior leads that repeated several times. Cardiovascular evaluation did not disclose any structural abnormality. Memory T wave following episodes of idiopathic left septal ventricular tachycardia was the reason of these changes and did not repeat after arrhythmia ablation.</AbstractText>
